{# The self-download control, shared by documents and decks.

   Placeholder for this task: only window.mountDownloadButton needs to exist
   yet, so the include-order test (stn-bd3.1) and the truth-table tests in
   tests/test_download.py can pass without the real capture-and-serialize
   behaviour, which is stn-bd3.4.

   Included strictly between _theme-toggle.html.j2 and _page-scripts.html.j2
   in both composition templates -- see tests/test_download.py for why that
   position is load-bearing: _page-scripts.html.j2 runs hljs.highlightAll()
   and the mermaid <pre> -> <div> swap at PARSE time, so the real
   implementation has to sit before it to capture the page's pristine markup.

   Two mount points, mirroring the theme toggle: a document gets the fixed
   container in html-template.html.j2; a deck's toolbar is built by JS at
   runtime, so _slide-scripts.html.j2 will call mountDownloadButton() once it
   inserts the theme group, the same way it already calls mountThemeToggle().

   No dollar sign anywhere in this file -- see _theme-toggle.html.j2, which
   this mirrors, and tests/test_download.py's
   test_the_partial_contains_no_pandoc_variable_syntax. #}
  <script>
  (function () {
    window.mountDownloadButton = function (container) {
      if (!container || container.querySelector('.download-button')) return;
      // Real capture-and-serialize behaviour lands in stn-bd3.4. This stub
      // exists so both composition templates have something safe to call.
      return null;
    };
  })();
  </script>
